                <p>
                  I'm <strong>S. Khavin</strong>, a final-year Computer Science Engineering student at
                  Sathyabama Institute of Science and Technology. My habit of taking systems apart to
                  see how they compute began around age seven building redstone and command-block
                  circuits in Minecraft, and now focuses on the internal computation of language and
                  vision-language models.
                </p>
                <p>
                  This line of work came from bottlenecks hit while building <em>AgentFox</em> (a
                  local agentic browser) and <em>Trinetra</em>: even with compressed visual inputs,
                  transformer inference remains quadratic, allocating the same compute for
                  <code>3 + 7</code> as for production code synthesis.
                </p>
